options.explanation:
$\begin{align}
\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left(-\dfrac{2x^3}{y}\right)
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{d}{dx}\left(\dfrac{2x^3}{y}\right)
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}(2x^3)\cdot y-2x^3\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dx}}{y^2}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{2\cdot(3x^2)\cdot y-2x^3\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dx}}{y^2}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{6x^2 y-2x^3\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dx}}{y^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-6x^2 y+2x^3\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dx}}{y^2}
\end{align}$

Now let's plug $\goldD{\dfrac{dy}{dx}=-\dfrac{2x^3}{y}}$ into the expression we got:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}&=\dfrac{-6x^2y+2x^3\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{dy}{dx}}}{y^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-6x^2y+2x^3\cdot\left(\goldD{-\dfrac{2x^3}{y}}\right)}{y^2}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{6x^2y^2+4x^6}{y^3}
\end{align}$

hints.content:
Finally, let's plug $\blueD{x=-2}$ and $\maroonD{y=1}$ into the expression we got:

$\begin{align}
\left.-\dfrac{6\blueD x^2\maroonD y^2+4\blueD x^6}{\maroonD y^3}\right\rvert_{(\blueD{-2},\maroonD{1})}&=-\dfrac{6(\blueD{-2})^2(\maroonD{1})^2+4(\blueD{-2})^6}{(\maroonD{1})^3}
\\\\
&=-280
\end{align}$
